{"created": "2026-07-16T14:27:23.291039+00:00", "modified": "2026-07-16T14:27:23.574806+00:00", "id": 21397474, "conceptrecid": "21397473", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.21397474", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.21397473", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21397474", "metadata": {"title": "Aurora-Lens: Proof and Precedence", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.21397474", "publication_date": "2026-07-16", "description": "<p class=\"PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer\">This evidence dossier records the authorship, chronology, public disclosure, and implementation history of the Aurora / Persistent Existence Frame (PEF) admissibility architecture and its software implementation, Aurora-Lens.</p>\n<p>The record begins in November 2025 and includes provisional patent filings, the separate <code>aurora-demo</code> and <code>Aurora-PEF</code> repository histories, GitHub-signed commits, dated public releases, direct circulation records, repository traffic evidence, PyPI publication, and live runtime deployment. Nine evidence artefacts are reproduced within the dossier, with SHA-256 digests provided in the evidence manifest. A supplementary provenance file records the Git ancestry and cryptographic verification of the November 2025 <code>aurora-demo</code> commits.</p>\n<p>The purpose of this deposit is narrow: to establish dated public authorship, conceptual precedence, implementation, and independent traceability for an architecture centred on persistent existence, admissibility before consequence, governed refusal, lawful continuation, authority preservation, and forensic auditability.</p>\n<p>This deposit does not claim that every later system or publication with adjacent terminology was derived from Aurora-Lens. Conceptual proximity, market convergence, institutional uptake, and direct derivation are separate questions.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Stokes, Margaret", "affiliation": null}], "keywords": ["Aurora-Lens", "Persistent Existence Frame", "PEF", "AI go